<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Egypt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> is the northern part of Egypt, consisting of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> and the area around Memphis. Its unification with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a> was the foundation of the Egyptian state, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaohs</a> bore the title of ruler of both lands. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, Lower Egypt was a key administrative region, and its fragmentation contributed to the period's decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lower-egypt.jpg" alt="Lower Egypt" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Dahl · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lower_Egypt_Nomes_01.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
